   "row": {
    "statement": "The UOVF is responsible for establishing and maintaining a system for collecting, evaluating and submitting to the authority information on adverse reactions, lack of efficacy, AEFIs and other safety/efficacy data on parallel-imported products and any data needed for risk-benefit assessment, including a quality system; preparing and submitting a regular safety report on request; and answering all authority requests with additional information needed for benefit-risk evaluation, including sales or exposure data.",
    "quote_en": "4. The UOVF in Ukraine have duties (but not limited to) regarding: 1) creation and maintenance of a system for collecting, evaluating and submitting to the state control body information on adverse reactions, lack of efficacy, AEFIs, other data related to the safety and efficacy of use of parallel-imported medicinal products, vaccines, tuberculin, as well as any data necessary for assessing the risk and benefit of use of the medicinal product, vaccine, tuberculin, including the quality system; 2) preparation and submission at the request of the state control body of a regular safety report; 3) providing, on all requests of the state control body, additional information necessary for assessing the benefit/risk balance of the parallel-imported medicinal product, vaccine, tuberculin, including data on sales volumes of the medicinal product or exposure of patients exposed to the parallel-imported medicinal product, vaccine, tuberculin;",
